    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d18">

                <pb facs="0130" n="18" sameAs="frus:frus1935v03/pg18"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.20/515: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Gauss</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peiping</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1935-01-25T12:00:00+08:00">January 25,
                        1935—noon</date>.<lb/>[Received January 25—4 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>35. The Military Attaché informs me that at a recent conversation in Shanghai
                    General Chiang Kai-shek urged that an American Army Air Force officer from the
                    active list be assigned as aviation adviser to China to take charge of the
                    Hangchow aviation school in succession to Jouett<anchor n="23" xml:id="d18-f1"/>
                    whose contract expires in June and who is not disposed to renew it. The Military
                    Attaché informed General Chiang that he is certain that the American Government
                    cannot entertain any such proposal.</p>
                <p>The Legation has reason to believe that an effort may be made through Jouett or
                    others to invite some fairly high ranking officer of the United States Army Air
                    Force now on the active list to retire and accept appointment as Jouett’s
                    successor.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Gauss</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d18-f1" n="23" xml:id="d18-f1-content">
                <p>Col. John H. Jouett, U. S. Army Reserve.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
